From 7f3e785b2ba782e72385570767841aa388e45299 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:08:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] B70-V32-HC3: hot/cold cold prefetch never runs under
 graph capture

apply_cold took the 0042 VRAM-staging path for any batch >= the prefetch
threshold (512), including the 512/1024-token captures. vLLM captures largest
first, so capture 1024 recorded the prefetcher side-stream events into the
graph and the next capture waited forever (ccs+bcs 100 %, all ranks). While the stream is capturing, apply_cold now
reads the cold experts over UVA (same kernel, same bytes, same math), with a
one-time log line; _load/acquire/release_and_prefetch raise if called during
capture, so a regression fails loudly instead of hanging. Eager prefill
chunks at or above the threshold keep the staging slots.

CPU: tests/model_executor/test_b70_hotcold_capture.py (9 passed; 6 of them
fail on the previous tree).
